OK, so `hasSelector` checks if the target or any ancestor (up to `domNode`) matches the selector. If the target has `nodrag`, the drag is not initiated.

Now, the issue might be that d3-drag still intercepts the mousedown event even when the drag is not initiated. Let me check the d3-drag behavior.

