        (!noDragClassName || !hasSelector(target, `.${noDragClassName}`, domNode)) &&
        (!handleSelector || hasSelector(target, handleSelector, domNode));
    return isDraggable;
});
```

If `isDraggable` is false, the filter returns false, and d3-drag doesn't start the drag. The mousedown event should propagate normally.

